      {
        "id": "urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ebded789f333203269fb1c1b3b286d68771b0a97.001.1",
        "event": "Flood Warning",
        "headline": "Flood Warning issued October 2 at 3:02AM AKDT until October 3 at 7:45AM AKDT by NWS Juneau AK",
        "description": "The second release from Suicide Basin is ongoing. Based on an\nobserved earlier start time of water draining from the basin, the\ncrest time for the Mendenhall Lake and River has been adjusted to\nearly Friday morning. Minor flooding is ongoing, and moderate\nflooding continues to be expected near Mendenhall Lake and River\nFriday morning.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding caused by a glacier-dammed lake outburst continues.\n\n* WHERE...The Mendenhall Lake And River near the Mendenhall Glacier\nRecreation area, View D",
        "severity": "Severe",
        "certainty": "Likely",
        "urgency": "Immediate",
        "sender": "NWS Juneau AK",
        "effective": "2026-10-02T03:02:00-08:00",
        "expires": "2026-10-02T11:15:00-08:00",
        "areas": "City and Borough of Juneau",
        "category": "Met",
        "response": "Avoid",
        "instruction": "Stay tuned to further developments by listening to your local radio,\ntelevision, or NOAA Weather Radio for further information.\n\nTurn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers ",
        "lat": 58.408181818181816,
        "lng": -134.56272727272727
      },
      {
        "id": "urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.042e8c3fdd62ff164ca15aafb038764260af4f6f.001.1",
